A feature is a ﬁeld that corresponds to the relevance of a document—for example, title,
overview, popularity score (number of views), and so on.
Build a feature set with a Mustache template for each feature. For more information about
features, see Working with Features.
In this example, we build a movie_features feature set with the title and overview ﬁelds:
POST _ltr/_featureset/movie_features
{
"featureset" : {
"name" : "movie_features",
"features" : [
{
"name" : "1",
"params" : [
"keywords"
],
"template_language" : "mustache",
"template" : {
"match" : {
"title" : "{{keywords}}"
}
}
},
{
"name" : "2",
"params" : [
"keywords"
],
"template_language" : "mustache",
"template" : {
"match" : {
"overview" : "{{keywords}}"
}
}
}
]
}
}
